    <h2>Discover the Flavors of Italy</h2>
    <h3>Pizza Margherita: A Classic Italian Delight</h3>
    
    <p>Pizza Margherita is a classic Italian dish from Naples, renowned for its simple yet bold flavors. This iconic pizza features a crisp, chewy crust topped with tangy tomato sauce, creamy mozzarella, and fresh basil.</p>
    
    <blockquote>
        <p><q>The key to a delicious Pizza Margherita lies in the balance of flavors – sweet tomato, creamy cheese, fresh basil, and a perfectly baked crust.</q></p>
        <footer>- Chef Marco, Italian Cuisine Expert</footer>
    </blockquote>
    
    <h3>Ingredients:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Pizza Dough:</strong> 300g</li>
        <li><strong>Tomato Sauce:</strong> 1/2 cup</li>
        <li><strong>Fresh Mozzarella:</strong> 200g</li>
        <li><strong>Fresh Basil:</strong> 10 leaves</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h3>Preparation:</h3>
    <ol>
        <li><em>Preheat the oven to 250°C for 15 minutes.</em></li>
        <li><em>Roll out the dough into a thin round base.</em></li>
        <li><em>Spread the tomato sauce evenly over the dough.</em></li>
        <li><em>Add torn mozzarella and bake for 8 to 10 minutes.</em></li>
        <li><em>Garnish with fresh basil and serve hot.</em></li>
    </ol>
    
    <h3>Cooking Tips:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><sup>1/4</sup> cup of olive oil drizzled on top adds authentic Italian flavor.</li>
        <li><sub>1</sub> teaspoon of sea salt in the dough gives the crust its signature taste.</li>
    </ul>
    
